  "name": "Add ChatIcon task types to subtask modal",
  "pinned": false,
  "description": "Here's a 5-line summary of the conversation:\n\n1. The task required adding all available task types to the subtask creation dropdown in the `codx-junior-ui` project's `ChatView.vue` component.\n2. The available chat modes (`chat`, `task`, `topic`, `vibe`, `prview`, `browser`, `slides`) were identified from the existing mode switcher dropdown in `ChatView.vue`.\n3. A `CHAT_MODES` constant array was added to `src/store/chats.js` and exposed via the store's state as `chatModes`, making it a single source of truth.\n4. The subtask modal's plain `<select>` dropdown was replaced with a visual grid of clickable mode cards, each using the `ChatIcon` component to display the appropriate icon alongside the mode label.\n5. The `chatModes` computed property in `ChatView.vue` was updated to reference `this.$chats.chatModes` from the store, ensuring consistency across the application.",
